INFO:agent.loop:\u26a1 Executing tool: 'knowledge_agent' with arguments: {"source_title": "Pandora Papers reporting on King Abdullah II property network", "source_url": "https://www.theguardian.com/news/2021/oct/03/king-of-jordan-hidden-property-empire-worth-more-than-100m-pandora-papers-reveal", "text": "Sources SRC-001 through SRC-004 report that Pandora Papers-linked records identify Jordan's King Abdullah II as beneficial owner/final beneficiary of offshore structures used to acquire overseas property. SRC-002 provides the most detailed account: a February 2017 Alcogal internal memorandum described Jordanian client Abdullah Al Hussein, born 30 January 1962 and linked to Raghadan Palace, as beneficial owner of 16 companies holding assets in the US, UK and Jersey. Named entities include Nabisco Holdings SA, Setara Limited and Timara Limited, which acquired three Malibu properties; additional entities held Washington DC and UK assets. SRC-002 reports three Malibu properties, the first bought August 2014 for $33.5m and two neighboring properties thereafter; three Washington DC condominiums bought in the prior two years for $13.8m total; and seven UK properties bought 2003-2011, including three in Belgravia, estimated current value about £28m. SRC-001 reports a different count/scope: 14 US/UK houses and flats acquired 2003-2017 for over €91m/$106m through 36 front companies registered in tax havens. SRC-003/SRC-004 report a network of offshore companies/tax havens and approximately $100m of property from Malibu to Washington DC and London; SRC-004 says Malibu mansions were purchased through three offshore companies for $68m, and mentions an Ascot house and multimillion-dollar central London apartments. Alcogal staff allegedly discussed avoiding identifying the beneficial owner as a politically exposed person and used 'you know who'; Alcogal denied deliberate failure and said identity was recorded in BVI's secure beneficial ownership system. The royal palace and DLA Piper denied impropriety, said properties were publicly known/held for privacy and security and official/private visits, and said all costs came from personal wealth, not state funds, aid or public treasury. Sources also state offshore ownership is not inherently illegal and no evidence of wrongdoing was reported. Jurisdictions mentioned include British Virgin Islands, Panama, Belize, Cyprus, UAE, Singapore, Switzerland, and Jersey; the detailed King-specific ownership link in SRC-002 is to BVI companies and assets in US, UK and Jersey. Advisers/service actors identified are Alcogal (Panamanian law firm) and DLA Piper (king's lawyers)."}
